  "takeaway": [
    "Own signals: Commits written with Claude Code → Coding-agent CLI downloads. Could be luck: the closest match is 4 weeks later (correlation +0.30, 77 weeks); in the first half of the history it was +0.41 and in the second half +0.17.",
    "Beyond OpenAI: Coding-agent CLI downloads (vs OpenAI) → npm downloads (vs OpenAI). Could be luck: the closest match is 8 weeks later (correlation -0.35, 60 weeks); in the first half of the history it was -0.56 and in the second half -0.16."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The closest pair of 12 own and 6 beyond-OpenAI pairs tested.",
    "A lead is one signal moving first and another following some weeks later, for example coding-agent CLI downloads picking up before SDK downloads do. Each bar is how closely the second signal's week-to-week changes matched the first's that many weeks earlier.",
    "Weekly growth has its own last two weeks removed, so a series that merely persists is not mistaken for a leader, and weeks are ranked, so one extreme week cannot decide the result.",
    "The grey band is what luck alone reaches for the best of 8 lags: 1,500 surrogate series with the same autocorrelation and random timing (fixed seed). It is corrected for how many pairs were tried before a pair is called anything but luck.",
    "Possible: survives the correction only. Holds up: survives it, holds in both halves of the history, and has at least 120 weeks. Could be luck: does not survive it.",
    "Weeks run Monday to Sunday and only complete weeks are used.",
    "Correlation is not cause. A lead shows what moved first, not why."
  ],
